mfc_open: fail with -ENODEV when the node has no device yet (docs 11.80)

__mfc_video_device_register() registers the node before video_set_drvdata(), and udev's v4l_id opens
it at once. mfc_open() then took the "no mfc device" exit with ret still 0, so the open succeeded
without a context and the close ran mfc_release() on a NULL context: kernel panic during boot.
--- a/mfc.c
+++ b/mfc.c
@@ -372,6 +372,7 @@ static int mfc_open(struct file *file)
 
 	if (!dev) {
 		mfc_pr_err("no mfc device to run\n");
+		ret = -ENODEV;
 		goto err_no_device;
 	}
 
